On Sunday, February 12, 2012 11:33:53 Remo Dentato wrote:
> {iY}. Oh! I thought that the schwa should never be stressed.

A schwa by itself is not, by default, stressed unless all vowels in the wor=
d=20
are schwas. A schwa in a diphthong can have the default stress.

In Albanian, the schwa is a normal vowel and can be stressed. We may want t=
o=20
borrow names from Albanian.

> It should be pronounced {bangrkor=C4=8Da} right? I just realized I don't
